  {
    "episode_id": 50313,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50313.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 87,
    "turn_text": "My friend, my friend Martin. He had these food stamps, which I had never seen him before in my life. My family didn't have them. And I looked at them and I thought there was monopoly money. It literally looked like monopoly money. And the different colors represented different bills, 20, 10, 5, and things like that. So he's showing me this stuff and I'm like, what, what is this? You know, it's like play money. He's like, no, we can buy food with this. I'm like, like, come on, it's you're messing with me here. He's like, watch, let's go to the grocery store, pick out whatever you want. I'm like, well, let's do it. So he took like $50 out of this pack because you could just rip them right out, like coupons almost. And we walked over right across from right, right live and he's like, get whatever you want. So we're walking around. and I'm getting like a bunch of American food because Mexican food. I love Mexican food, don't get me wrong, but after a while you just wanted to have some sloppy joes or something different. And so I'm like picking out all these different items and then I got some candy and I was like, no, candy, no, you can't get the candy. I'm like, okay, fine. But at the moment, I honestly thought he was joking. I said, well, let's see how far we can go with this joke. And so I fill up the card, he's adding it up, It's about 40 something dollars and now we take it to the cashier. The cashier does all the items. He pulls out the money and I'm looking at her. I'm looking at the cashier. I'm like, okay, I can't wait to see her face. All of a sudden she takes the money. I'm like, wait a minute. She's taking the money. This is wow. And then all of a sudden she opens up the register and she pulls out change using more of that colored money. I'm like, what? Funny money was like what is this like monopoly money and then she pulls out some coins They were like little blue chips for 50 cents and I a bunch of different colors. I'm like you gotta be kidding me This is real so I'm like, okay, and Martin's like let's go. I'm like Wow, this is amazing So I had two bags of groceries going to my house. I see my mom I'm like mom. Look at look at all this grocery. She's all I'm all excited like where did you get this and then I see my dad Coming from, you know, from the side drive. And I go, Martin, and look, we use this money. And oh, boy, she said something like, you have to call me that kid. Oh, no, to papa. Oh, it was like that. It was like, oh, it was like boom, boom, boom. And I'm like, and then I don't know what, all I knew was that we were getting good food. And so I wasn't really listening to her. And I got excited. I showed it to my dad.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
